5. **Eggs remaining to sell**: 
   $$
   16 \text{ (total eggs)} - 7 \text{ (consumed)} = 9 \text{ eggs}
   $$

6. **Earnings from selling eggs**: Each egg is sold for $2, so:
   $$
   9 \text{ eggs} \times 2 \text{ dollars/egg} = 18 \text{ dollars}
   $$

Thus, Janet makes **$\boxed{18}$** dollars every day at the farmers' market. 
