First, we calculate the total daily feed required for all chickens. Wendi has 20 chickens, and each chicken gets 3 cups per day. So the total feed required for the day is:

$$
20 \text{ chickens} \times 3 \text{ cups per chicken} = 60 \text{ cups}
$$

Wendi has already given 15 cups in the morning and 25 cups in the afternoon, so the amount of feed given so far is:

$$
15 \text{ cups} + 25 \text{ cups} = 40 \text{ cups}
$$

To find the amount needed for the final meal, we subtract the amount already given from the total required:

$$
60 \text{ cups} - 40 \text{ cups} = 20 \text{ cups}
$$

Therefore, Wendi needs to give her chickens 20 cups of feed in the final meal of the day. 

