First, let's break down the hours. She works 40 hours at the regular rate. Then, she has 5 hours of overtime. So, the regular pay is 40 hours times $10. That gives us 400 dollars. Then, the overtime pay is 5 hours times 1.2 times $10. 1.2 times $10 is $12, so 5 hours times 12 is 60 dollars. Then, adding those two amounts together, 400 plus 60 equals 460 dollars. Therefore, Eliza's earnings for the week are $460.
