First, the first 3 customers each buy one DVD. So, 3 customers times 1 DVD each would be 3 DVDs. Then, the next 2 customers buy 2 DVDs each. Hmm, so 2 customers multiplied by 2 DVDs each is 4 DVDs. Wait, 2 times 2 is 4? Yeah, that seems right. 

Then, the last 3 customers don't buy any DVDs. So that's 0 DVDs from those. 

Now, adding them all up: the first part was 3 DVDs, then 4 more from the next customers, and then 0 from the last ones. So 3 plus 4 is 7. And then adding 0 doesn't change it. So total DVDs sold on Tuesday should be 7?

