The problem involves calculating the total number of pie pieces and determining how many were taken by the guests based on the remaining pieces.

**Step 1: Calculate Total Pieces of Pie**  
Grandma baked 5 pies, and each pie was cut into 8 pieces.  
$$
\text{Total pieces} = 5 \text{ pies} \times 8 \text{ pieces per pie} = 40 \text{ pieces}
$$

**Step 2: Determine Pieces Taken by Guests**  
At the end of the evening, 14 pieces of pie remained. To find the number of pieces taken by the guests, subtract the remaining pieces from the total pieces:  
$$
\text{Pieces taken} = 40 \text{ total pieces} - 14 \text{ remaining pieces} = 26 \text{ pieces}
$$

**Final Answer:**  
$$
\boxed{26}
$$

The guests took **26** pieces of pie.  
\boxed{26}  
