Answer: \boxed{294} The problem is asking how much money Lloyd makes per week from selling eggs.

1. **Eggs produced per week:**  
   Lloyd's chickens produce 252 eggs per day.  
   Over 7 days, this is:  
   $$
   252 \, \text{eggs/day} \times 7 \, \text{days} = 1764 \, \text{eggs/week}
   $$

2. **Convert eggs to dozens:**  
   Since 1 dozen = 12 eggs:  
   $$
   \frac{1764}{12} = 147 \, \text{dozens}
   $$

3. **Calculate weekly income:**  
   Eggs are sold at $2 per dozen:  
   $$
   147 \, \text{dozens} \times 2 \, \text{\$/dozen} = 294 \, \text{\$}
   $$

Thus, Lloyd makes **$294** per week from selling eggs.  
