The problem is asking how many toys Uriah needs to remove to reduce the weight of his book bag by 15 pounds. We know that each comic book weighs 1/4 pound and each toy weighs 1/2 pound. He removes 30 comic books.

First, calculate the total weight of the comic books:
$$
30 \times \frac{1}{4} = 7.5 \text{ pounds}
$$

Next, determine the remaining weight to be removed:
$$
15 - 7.5 = 7.5 \text{ pounds}
$$

Now, find how many toys are needed to remove 7.5 pounds. Since each toy weighs 1/2 pound:
$$
7.5 \div \frac{1}{2} = 7.5 \times 2 = 15
$$

Thus, Uriah needs to remove $\boxed{15}$ toys. 

Answer: $\boxed{15}$

