Hmm, so if I divide the total amount of money he has by the cost per movie trip, that should give me the number of times he can go. Let me write that out: 42 divided by 14. Let me do that calculation. 14 times 3 is 42, right? Because 14 times 2 is 28, and 14 times 3 is 28 + 14 = 42. So 42 divided by 14 is 3. 

