Cecilia needs to calculate the total amount of dog food required for her puppy in the first year. 

**Step 1: Determine the number of days in the first 180 days**  
The puppy is fed **1 cup per day** for the first **180 days**.  
$$
180 \text{ days} \times 1 \text{ cup/day} = 180 \text{ cups}
$$

**Step 2: Determine the number of days in the remaining portion of the year**  
After the first 180 days, the puppy is fed **2 cups per day** for the remaining $365 - 180 = 185$ days.  
$$
185 \text{ days} \times 2 \text{ cups/day} = 370 \text{ cups}
$$

**Step 3: Calculate total cups of dog food required**  
$$
180 \text{ cups} + 370 \text{ cups} = 550 \text{ cups}
$$

**Step 4: Calculate the number of bags needed**  
Each bag contains **110 cups**, so the number of bags is:  
$$
\frac{550 \text{ cups}}{110 \text{ cups/bag}} = 5 \text{ bags}
$$

Thus, Cecilia will use $\boxed{5}$ bags of dog food in the first year.  
$$
\boxed{5}
$$
