### Step 1: Calculate the number of years Gene has been vacationing

He started vacationing at age 23 and is now 34. The total number of years he has been vacationing is:

$$
34 - 23 = 11 \text{ years}
$$

---

### Step 2: Calculate the total number of t-shirts (quilt blocks)

Each year he goes on 4 vacations, and each vacation results in one t-shirt (quilt block). Therefore, the total number of quilt blocks is:

$$
11 \text{ years} \times 4 \text{ vacations/year} = 44 \text{ quilt blocks}
$$

