$$
5 \, \text{children} \times 5 \, \text{lbs} = 25 \, \text{lbs}
$$

Finally, we add the amounts for the adults and the children to find the total amount of potato salad needed:
$$
200 \, \text{lbs} + 25 \, \text{lbs} = 225 \, \text{lbs}
$$

Therefore, Ted needs to bring $\boxed{225}$ pounds of potato salad to the picnic to feed everyone.
