Alright, let me break this down. First, the sauce volume is 32 ounces, but that's after cooking. Since the tomatoes lose half their volume during cooking, that means the original volume of tomatoes before cooking must be double the volume of the sauce. So, if the sauce is 32 ounces, then the original volume of tomatoes was 32 * 2 = 64 ounces. Is that right? Wait, because when you cook them, the volume is halved. So the original volume times 1/2 equals the sauce volume. So original volume is sauce volume times 2. So yes, 32 * 2 = 64 ounces of tomatoes before cooking.

