The problem involves calculating the number of tomatoes Freda used to make 32 ounces of sauce, considering that each can of tomatoes loses half its volume when cooked into sauce.

**Step 1: Understand the relationship between can volume and sauce volume.**  
Each can contains 16 ounces of tomatoes, and when cooked, they lose half their volume. Therefore, each can of tomatoes produces:  
$$
\frac{16}{2} = 8 \text{ ounces of sauce}.
